    "created_at": "2017-09-10T23:24:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-10T23:25:45Z",
    "body": "I think more interesting test would be with content using Big5 and UTF-8 text encodings in Chinese & Japanese. e.g. some of shared hosting services in Japan used to serve all text/* files as EUC-JP even if the content was actually in Shift_JIS (or Microsoft CP932) or vice versa. I wouldn't be surprised even if those websites had to specify a different text encoding scheme on cross-origin scripts they're importing.\r\n\r\nAt minimum, it's worth checking whether the text encoding of the imported script differs from that of the importer website, and get statistics of what kind of non-unicode text encodings are commonly used. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
