    "updated_at": "2017-09-11T09:59:33Z",
    "body": "Inheriting the encoding seems about as problematic as the attribute, correct?\r\n\r\nThe encodings specified in `charset` attribute where that is different from `pageGuessedCharset`:\r\n```\r\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS num, elementCharset FROM (\r\n  SELECT * FROM [pelagic-breaker-785:test.link_script_all]\r\n  WHERE LOWER(pageGuessedCharset) != elementCharset\r\n)\r\nGROUP BY elementCharset\r\nORDER BY num DESC\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nRow | num | elementCharset |  \r\n-- | -- | -- | --\r\n1 | 26536 | utf-8 |  \r\n2 | 876 | windows-1251 |  \r\n3 | 530 | iso-8859-1 |  \r\n4 | 465 | gb2312 |  \r\n5 | 280 | gbk |  \r\n6 | 129 | shift_jis |  \r\n7 | 52 | utf8 |  \r\n8 | 42 | euc-jp |  \r\n9 | 41 | gb18030 |  \r\n10 | 24 | euc-kr |  \r\n11 | 20 | windows-1252 |  \r\n12 | 15 | iso-8859-2 |  \r\n13 | 13 | big5 |  \r\n14 | 6 | windows-1250 |  \r\n15 | 5 | shift-jis |  \r\n16 | 3 | sjis |  \r\n17 | 3 | windows-1254 |  \r\n18 | 2 | utf- |  \r\n19 | 2 | iso-8859-15 |  \r\n20 | 2 | utf-4 |  \r\n21 | 2 | shit_jis |  \r\n22 | 1 | uft-8 |  \r\n23 | 1 | iso-8859-8 |  \r\n24 | 1 | windows-1257 |  \r\n25 | 1 | iso-8859- |  \r\n26 | 1 | urf-8 |  \r\n27 | 1 | cp1251 |  \r\n28 | 1 | unf-8 |  \r\n29 | 1 | shif_jis |  \r\n30 | 1 | charset |  \r\n",
