    "created_at": "2017-09-11T11:59:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-11T11:59:16Z",
    "body": "To play devil's advocate for a bit: The effect of a page causing JS or CSS that will run/apply in its own context to be mangled isn't necessarily dangerous the way mangling an HTML page in an iframe would be. Therefore, it's not clear that it's necessary to prevent cross-origin encoding overrides.",
